[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Class 3 Multi Segment with Untrusted Wired Connection Security Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @vcr_grammar

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This section specifies cybersecurity requirements for Class 3 vehicle components: **Multi Segment with Untrusted Wired Connection**.

Class 3 devices are truck modules connected to two or more vehicle network segments, at least one of which is an Untrustworthy Network Domain (UND), that do not perform Boundary Gateway or Untrustworthy Gateway behaviors but could perform Boundary Gateway behaviors if controlled by an attacker (a Boundary Potential Pivot). Examples include modules connected to diagnostic ports, trailer bridges, or networks exposed to external physical connections.

Examples include:
- Tractor/Trailer Bridge #1 / #2 (J1939 SA 32, 138, 39)
- Powertrain Control Module (CPC) (J1939 SA 90)
- Engine #1 (MCM / EMS / ECM) (J1939 SA 00, 01)
- Transmission #1 (TCM) (J1939 SA 03)
- Cab Controller Primary / Secondary (SAM CAB) (J1939 SA 49, 50)
- Instrument Cluster #1 (Gauges) (J1939 SA 23)
- On Board Diagnostic Unit (J1939 SA 250)
- ADAS Adaptive Cruise Control / Lane Keep (Bendix Fusion) (J1939 SA 42, 232, 19)
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Baseline Security Requirements Applicability

